*__pycache__

# Local environment and downloaded market data
.venv/
venv/
app/cache/
app/runs/
.pytest_cache/

# .streamlit/config.toml IS committed — it carries the app's theme.
# Secrets never are.
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# Personal financial data — real positions, cost basis, and every trade
# ever entered against them. Never commit.
app/holdings.json
app/transactions.json

# --- V2 alpha research: derived data, deliberately not versioned. ---
# Excluded at programme closure because each is regenerable from committed code
# and too large to version (alpha/cache/ ~171 MB of vendor CSVs; panel.pkl 212 MB).
# The SHA-256 of every excluded artefact is recorded in
# reports/V2_3_EVIDENCE_MANIFEST.md, so an excluded file stays identifiable even
# though it is not stored here. Rebuild path is in
# reports/V2_3_REPRODUCTION_CHECKLIST.md.
alpha/cache/
alpha/out/panel.pkl
alpha/out/run1_dead_ret_12_1/development.pkl

# --- V3 filings research: raw EDGAR bulk archives and the derived facts
# table. Regenerable: the zips re-download from sec.gov (URLs in
# alpha/build_filings.py) and facts.parquet rebuilds from them via
# `python -m alpha.build_filings`. filings_meta.json (small, the build's
# fingerprint) IS committed, like panel_meta.json.
alpha/edgar/*.zip
alpha/edgar/facts.parquet
# company_tickers.json is re-fetched by the build when absent, and the mapping
# it actually produced is pinned in filings_meta.json's symbol_to_cik - which
# is the reproducibility-relevant record, since the SEC's live map changes.
alpha/edgar/company_tickers.json

# --- V3 Family 2: the SEC insider-transaction bulk archives (426 MB) and the
# derived purchase table. Regenerable exactly like the filings ones: the zips
# re-download from sec.gov (URL in reports/FAMILY2_ADMISSIBILITY.md) and the
# parquet rebuilds via `python -m alpha.build_insider`. insider_meta.json
# (small, the build's fingerprint) IS committed, like filings_meta.json.
alpha/edgar/insider/
alpha/edgar/insider_purchases.parquet
